{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1428042-geist-and-changeling-crossover-questions","id":1428042,"title":"Geist and Changeling Crossover Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-10T17:39:37-08:00","id":1428042,"title":"Geist and Changeling Crossover Questions","content":"Hi there. After spending quite a bit of time lurking, I've decided to ask make an account and ask a few questions for some crossover interactions between a sluagh and a sin-eater.<br /> <br /> I vaguely recall from the 20th anniversary edition that humans aren't &quot;supposed&quot; to know about the kith, and I believe there's also something in that stating the Mists wouldn't affect supernatural beings. The Mists usually take care of any memories a mortal would have of The Dreaming, so a sin-eater would likely keep their memories, wouldn't they?<br /> Since sin-eaters and sluagh can communicate with the dead (wraiths and so on), would a sin-eater potentially be a target knowing about the kith and interacting with an individual sluagh<br /> Though they largely keep to themselves, sluagh tend to exchange their secrets as currency; aside from their own networks, is there anything like the Masquerade that would prevent a sluagh and a sin-eater from continuing to work together?<br /> Would the Mists reject a sin-eater attempting to get through?<br /> <br /> Mind you, this is within a homebrew setting. I've got the core CtD book and the Sluagh book, but I wasn't sure if there were any other sourcebooks that would have the information. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26571-redshirtmook","name":"RedShirtMook","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T15:32:05-08:00","id":1428127,"title":"","content":"If course it's in a homebrew setting. Sluagh and Sin-Eaters don't live in the same universe: Sluagh are from the World of Darkness, and Sin-Eaters are from the Chronicles of Darkness. Having a Sluagh meet up with a Sin-Eater would be like having Batman encounter Black Panther. <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, the closest thing there is to a Sin-Eater is <b>Wraith</b>'s Risen; and they're more blatantly undead than the Sin-Eaters are. Conversely, the closest thing to the Kithain in the Chronicles of Darkness are the protagonists of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>; and they're a very different take on what a changeling is. <br /> <br /> All that said, Batman and Black Panther would be a cool team-up. Likewise, mixing the World of Darkness and the Chronicles of Darkness has the potential to be cool, too. If you're going to mix them, I'd say that Sin-Eaters should be as immune to the Mists as the Risen are. Which, I believe, is \u201cthey're as immune to the Mists as the Storyteller wants them to be\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T15:43:37-08:00","id":1428128,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I Liked your explanation of the two universes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}